<a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-label-sm font-label-sm border-b border-surface-cream/30 hover:border-surface-cream transition-all" href="#">
                            Contact Us <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm">arrow_forward</span>
</a>
</div>
</div>
</aside>
<!-- Accordion Section -->
<div class="lg:col-span-9 space-y-16">
<!-- Category: Daily Care -->
<section id="daily-care">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8 border-b border-outline-variant/20 pb-4">
<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-heritage-crimson/10 flex items-center justify-center text-heritage-crimson">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined">cleaning_services</span>
</div>
<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-architectural-blue">Daily Care</h2>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4">
<!-- FAQ Item 1 -->
<div class="accordion-item bg-white border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 hover:border-heritage-crimson/30">
<button class="w-full px-6 py-5 flex justify-between items-center text-left focus:outline-none" onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
<span class="font-body-lg font-bold text-on-surface">How do I clean my tiles daily?</span>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-chevron transition-transform text-on-surface-variant">expand_more</span>
</button>
<div class="accordion-content px-6">
<p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
                                    For daily maintenance, simply use a soft broom or microfiber mop to remove dust and grit. If needed, damp mop with clean water and a pH-neutral cleaner. Avoid excessive water, as Athangudi tiles are handcrafted cement and prefer controlled moisture.
                                </p>
</div>
</div>
<!-- FAQ Item 2 -->
<div class="accordion-item bg-white border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 hover:border-heritage-crimson/30">
<button class="w-full px-6 py-5 flex justify-between items-center text-left focus:outline-none" onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
<span class="font-body-lg font-bold text-on-surface">Can I use a vacuum on my tiles?</span>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-chevron transition-transform text-on-surface-variant">expand_more</span>
</button>
<div class="accordion-content px-6">
<p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
                                    Yes, you can use a vacuum, but ensure it has a soft brush attachment or "hard floor" setting. Avoid vacuum cleaners with rotating beater bars, as they can cause micro-scratches on the polished surface of the cement tiles over time.
                                </p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Category: Deep Cleaning -->
<section id="deep-cleaning">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8 border-b border-outline-variant/20 pb-4">
<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-heritage-crimson/10 flex items-center justify-center text-heritage-crimson">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined">sanitizer</span>
</div>
<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-architectural-blue">Deep Cleaning</h2>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4">
<div class="accordion-item bg-white border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 hover:border-heritage-crimson/30">
<button class="w-full px-6 py-5 flex justify-between items-center text-left focus:outline-none" onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
<span class="font-body-lg font-bold text-on-surface">What cleaning agents are safe?</span>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-chevron transition-transform text-on-surface-variant">expand_more</span>
</button>
<div class="accordion-content px-6">
<p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
                                    Only use pH-neutral cleaners specifically formulated for natural stone or cement tiles. <strong>Avoid</strong> acidic cleaners (like vinegar or lemon juice) and harsh bleaches, as these will etch the cement and dull the vibrant patterns. We recommend a simple mixture of mild soap and lukewarm water for periodic deep cleaning.
                                </p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Category: Stain Removal -->
<section id="stain-removal">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8 border-b border-outline-variant/20 pb-4">
<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-heritage-crimson/10 flex items-center justify-center text-heritage-crimson">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined">ink_eraser</span>
</div>
<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-architectural-blue">Stain Removal</h2>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4">
<div class="accordion-item bg-white border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 hover:border-heritage-crimson/30">
<button class="w-full px-6 py-5 flex justify-between items-center text-left focus:outline-none" onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
<span class="font-body-lg font-bold text-on-surface">How do I remove coffee or wine stains?</span>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-chevron transition-transform text-on-surface-variant">expand_more</span>
</button>
<div class="accordion-content px-6">
<p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                    Blot the spill immediately with a soft cloth—do not rub. For persistent stains:
                                </p>
<ul class="list-disc ml-6 space-y-2 text-on-surface-variant">
<li>Apply a paste of baking soda and water.</li>
<li>Let it sit for 15-20 minutes.</li>
<li>Gently wipe away with a damp cloth.</li>
</ul>
<p class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed italic">
                                    Note: Athangudi tiles are porous. Prompt action is the best defense against staining.
                                </p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</div>
</div>
<!-- Visual Decorative Element -->
<div class="mt-32 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-base opacity-40 grayscale hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-700">
